  "stories": {
    "systems": {
      "text": "eylül learned systems by running them. with ARAMA she coordinated {{giy|GİY}}, an education platform for students; at {{bayetav|BAYETAV Art}} she went from running events to shaping how the whole space worked. now she maps learning paths into a tool at the university of wuppertal: {{lernpfad|Lernpfad-Designer}}.",
      "works": [
        "giy",
        "bayetav",
        "cologne",
        "lernpfad"
      ]
    },
    "learning": {
      "text": "it started with a course in applied drama: learning by doing. at {{giy|GİY}} she designed learning materials and workshops for students, and her thesis {{inner-mechanics|the institute of inner mechanics}} asks how creative education can make room for introspection. today she builds {{lernpfad|Lernpfad-Designer}} at the university of wuppertal.",
      "works": [
        "giy",
        "inner-mechanics",
        "lernpfad",
        "fake-news-mystery"
      ]
    },
    "visual": {
      "text": "visual communication design was her first language, and she still speaks it every day. since 2019 she has designed identities, publications and websites as a freelancer, and the {{publications|reports and books}} of BAYETAV. her way of working: understanding complexity → structuring ideas → visualizing clarity.",
      "works": [
        "publications",
        "giy",
        "motif",
        "so-fi"
      ]
    },
    "art": {
      "text": "she makes things by hand, usually with others: letterpress at {{fuar-matbaasi|Fuar Matbaası}}, an installation like {{motif|Motif}}, exhibitions at BAYETAV Art. today her small studio is at the Hidden Agenda Collective, among artists and designers from many fields. at KISD she builds speculative worlds, like {{inner-mechanics|a fictional institute}}.",
      "works": [
        "motif",
        "inner-mechanics",
        "fuar-matbaasi",
        "memo"
      ]
    },
    "research": {
      "text": "cultural studies came first, then fieldwork in places like {{abacioglu|Abacıoğlu Han}}, then a few years of sociology. at KISD she studies how people trust public data in {{cologne|Customer Centers of the Future}} and how education feels from the inside in {{refinding-kisd|Refin(d)ing KISD}}. for her, data is never just technical: it is cultural, emotional and human.",
      "works": [
        "inner-mechanics",
        "cologne",
        "refinding-kisd",
        "abacioglu"
      ]
    }
  },
